WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.877
A strong data preparation design often keeps several logical layers.

00:00:04.877 --> 00:00:09.772
The raw table preserves source records with little or no modification.

00:00:09.772 --> 00:00:19.017
A clean view provides reusable transformations for analysis, such as normalized names, emails, and phone numbers.

00:00:19.017 --> 00:00:23.419
A quality view exposes issue flags and review logic.

00:00:23.997 --> 00:00:28.809
Downstream users can then choose the layer appropriate for their task.

00:00:28.809 --> 00:00:34.234
For example, an analyst building a dashboard may use the clean view.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:38.989
A data steward investigating problems may use the quality view.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:41.874
An auditor may need the raw table.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:47.884
This layered approach is safer than repeatedly overwriting the same source columns.

00:00:47.884 --> 00:00:55.874
It also makes your pipeline easier to explain: raw data came in here, standardization happened here,

00:00:55.874 --> 00:00:58.339
and quality rules were applied here.
